module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.AlmostBlowUp.AffineAlmostBlowUpCriterion
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.HTopology.AlmostBlowUpSheafCriterion
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.HTopology.AlmostBlowUpSheafInduction
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.HTopology.FppfHComparison

/-!
# The essential image of `Rε_*` on the big fppf site, tested on affine almost blowup squares

Stacks 0EWQ says that an object `K` of `D⁺(𝒪_{fppf})` lies in the essential image of the derived
direct image `Rε_*` along the comparison of ringed sites `ε : (C_h, 𝒪_h) ⟶ (C_{fppf}, 𝒪_{fppf})`
if and only if the canonical Mayer–Vietoris comparison `c^K_{X,X',Z,E}` of Stacks 0F16 is a
quasi-isomorphism for every almost blowup square of the site whose base `X` is affine.  The big h
site and the big fppf site of Stacks 0EU1 have the same underlying category `C`, so the assertion
is `AlgebraicGeometry.EssImageIffAffineAlmostBlowUpBigH` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.AlmostBlowUp.AffineAlmostBlowUpCriterion` for the
fppf topology on that category, and that topology is built here.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.fppfPrecoverage` and `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.fppfTopology`: the
  fppf topology on the big h category over `S`, generated by the families of morphisms of the site
  whose underlying family of morphisms of schemes is an fppf covering.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.fppfTopology_le_topology`: the fppf topology on the big h category
  over `S` is coarser than the h topology.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.isZariskiSheaf_of_isFppfSheaf` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.isAffineFlatProperFinitePresentationSheaf_of_isFppfSheaf`: an fppf
  sheaf of sets satisfies conditions (1) and (2) of Stacks 0EVF.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.isSheaf_of_isFppfSheaf_of_isAffineAlmostBlowUpSheaf`: an fppf sheaf
  of sets satisfying condition (3) of Stacks 0EVF is a sheaf for the h topology.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.isAffineAlmostBlowUpDetecting_fppfTopology`: affine almost blowup
  squares detect h sheaves among fppf sheaves of sets.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.essImage_iff_forall_isCSquareIso_affineAlmostBlowUp_fppf_bigH`: **Stacks
  0EWQ** for the fppf topology, the setting of the source.

## Implementation notes

**The fppf topology on the big h category.**  It is built in the shape of
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.zariskiTopology`: the precoverage collects the presieves of the
families of morphisms of the site whose image under `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.toScheme` lies in
Mathlib's `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.fppfPrecoverage`, and the topology is the one it generates.
The h topology on the same category remains `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.topology` and nothing
about it is redefined.  The cardinality cutoff of the chosen big h site is no obstruction to
comparing the two topologies: `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.sieve₀_mem_topology_of_isHCovering`
carries an arbitrary h covering family of the site to a covering sieve of the h topology, finding
a bounded representative of it inside the site, and an fppf covering is an h covering by
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsHCovering.of_mem_fppfPrecoverage`, Stacks 0ETV.

**Detection.**  An fppf sheaf of sets satisfies condition (1) of Stacks 0EVF because a Zariski
covering of schemes is an fppf covering, and condition (2) because a flat proper surjective
morphism of finite presentation is an fppf covering all by itself — properness is not used for
that, only flatness, surjectivity and local finite presentation.  The sufficiency direction of
Stacks 0EVF,
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.isSheaf_of_zariski_and_affineFlatProperFP_and_affineAlmostBlowUp`,
then turns condition (3) into the h sheaf condition, which is exactly
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.IsAffineAlmostBlowUpDetecting` for the fppf topology.

**The two forms of condition (3).**  The detection condition is phrased on the square-indexed
family `AlgebraicGeometry.AffineAlmostBlowUpSquare`, condition (3) of Stacks 0EVF on the data of
Stacks 0EVD.  The two differ by `CategoryTheory.IsPullback.flip`, once on the square of the site
and once on its image, because `CategoryTheory.Square.IsPullback` reads the two legs of a square
in the order opposite to the one Stacks 0EVD states them in, and `CategoryTheory.Square.op`
exchanges the two outer vertices.  The commutativity of the square of the site is recovered from
the commutativity of its image, the underlying-scheme functor being faithful.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EWQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EWQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EVF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EVF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EVD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EVD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0ETV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ETV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EU1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EU1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F16](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F16)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F18](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F18)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u v r

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

namespace BigHOver

variable (B : BigHSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-! ### The fppf topology on the big h category over `S` -/

/-- The fppf precoverage on the big h category over `S`: a presieve is covering when it is the
presieve of a family of morphisms of the site whose underlying family of morphisms of schemes is
an fppf covering.

This is the shape of `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.zariskiPrecoverage`, with Mathlib's
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.fppfPrecoverage` in place of the Zariski one. -/
def fppfPrecoverage : Precoverage (BigHOver B S hS) where
  coverings X := {R | ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} X, E.presieve₀ = R ∧
    (E.map (BigHOver.toScheme B S hS)).presieve₀ ∈
      Scheme.fppfPrecoverage ((BigHOver.toScheme B S hS).obj X)}

/-- **The fppf topology on the big h category over `S`.** The Grothendieck topology generated by
the families of morphisms of the site whose underlying family of morphisms of schemes is an fppf
covering.

This is the topology of the big fppf site of Stacks 0EU1 on the underlying category of the big h
site.  The h topology on that category is `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.topology`. -/
abbrev fppfTopology : GrothendieckTopology (BigHOver B S hS) :=
  (fppfPrecoverage B S hS).toGrothendieck

/-- The fppf topology on the big h category over `S` is coarser than the h topology.

An fppf covering is an h covering by Stacks 0ETV,
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsHCovering.of_mem_fppfPrecoverage`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.sieve₀_mem_topology_of_isHCovering` turns that into membership of the
h topology. -/
theorem fppfTopology_le_topology :
    fppfTopology B S hS ≤ BigHOver.topology B S hS := by
  rw [Precoverage.toGrothendieck_le_iff_le_toPrecoverage]
  rintro X R ⟨E, rfl, hE⟩
  rw [GrothendieckTopology.mem_toPrecoverage_iff]
  exact sieve₀_mem_topology_of_isHCovering B S hS E
    (IsHCovering.of_mem_fppfPrecoverage _ _ hE)

/-! ### An fppf sheaf satisfies the first two conditions of Stacks 0EVF -/

variable (F : (BigHOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type v)

/-- An fppf sheaf on the big h category over `S` satisfies the sheaf condition for every family
of morphisms of the site whose underlying family of morphisms of schemes is an fppf covering. -/
theorem isSheafFor_of_mem_fppfPrecoverage
    (hF : Presheaf.IsSheaf (fppfTopology B S hS) F)
    {X : BigHOver B S hS} (E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} X)
    (hE : (E.map (BigHOver.toScheme B S hS)).presieve₀ ∈
      Scheme.fppfPrecoverage ((BigHOver.toScheme B S hS).obj X)) :
    Presieve.IsSheafFor F E.presieve₀ := by
  rw [Presieve.isSheafFor_iff_generate]
  exact hF.isSheafFor _ ((fppfPrecoverage B S hS).generate_mem_toGrothendieck ⟨E, rfl, hE⟩)

/-- **Condition (1) of Stacks 0EVF for an fppf sheaf.** An fppf sheaf on the big h category over
`S` is a sheaf for the Zariski topology: a Zariski covering of schemes is an fppf covering, by
Stacks 021N. -/
theorem isZariskiSheaf_of_isFppfSheaf (hF : Presheaf.IsSheaf (fppfTopology B S hS) F) :
    BigHOver.IsZariskiSheaf B S hS F := fun _ E hE ↦
  isSheafFor_of_mem_fppfPrecoverage B S hS F hF E
    (Scheme.zariskiPrecoverage_le_fppfPrecoverage _ hE)

/-- **Condition (2) of Stacks 0EVF for an fppf sheaf.** An fppf sheaf on the big h category over
`S` satisfies the sheaf condition for the one-element family attached to a morphism of the site
with affine target which is flat, proper, surjective and of finite presentation.

Neither affineness of the target nor properness is used: such a morphism is flat, surjective and
locally of finite presentation, which makes it an fppf covering all by itself. -/
theorem isAffineFlatProperFinitePresentationSheaf_of_isFppfSheaf
    (hF : Presheaf.IsSheaf (fppfTopology B S hS) F) :
    BigHOver.IsAffineFlatProperFinitePresentationSheaf B S hS F := by
  intro X Y f _ hflat _ hsurj hfp
  have hE : ((PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{u + 1} f).map
      (BigHOver.toScheme B S hS)).presieve₀ ∈
      Scheme.fppfPrecoverage ((BigHOver.toScheme B S hS).obj X) := by
    rw [PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀, Scheme.fppfPrecoverage,
      Scheme.ofArrows_mem_precoverage_iff]
    exact ⟨fun x ↦ ⟨PUnit.unit, hsurj.1 x⟩, fun _ ↦ ⟨hflat, hfp.1⟩⟩
  have hFor := isSheafFor_of_mem_fppfPrecoverage B S hS F hF
    (PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{u + 1} f) hE
  rwa [PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_singleton] at hFor

/-! ### Affine almost blowup squares detect h sheaves among fppf sheaves -/

/-- **Stacks 0EVF for the fppf topology.** An fppf sheaf of sets on the big h category over `S`
which sends every almost blowup square of the site with affine base to a cartesian square of sets
is a sheaf for the h topology.

Conditions (1) and (2) of Stacks 0EVF hold for an fppf sheaf, so this is the sufficiency direction
of that tag,
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.isSheaf_of_zariski_and_affineFlatProperFP_and_affineAlmostBlowUp`. -/
theorem isSheaf_of_isFppfSheaf_of_isAffineAlmostBlowUpSheaf
    (hF : Presheaf.IsSheaf (fppfTopology B S hS) F)
    (h3 : BigHOver.IsAffineAlmostBlowUpSheaf B S hS F) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (BigHOver.topology B S hS) F :=
  isSheaf_of_zariski_and_affineFlatProperFP_and_affineAlmostBlowUp B S hS F
    (isZariskiSheaf_of_isFppfSheaf B S hS F hF)
    (isAffineFlatProperFinitePresentationSheaf_of_isFppfSheaf B S hS F hF) h3

/-- **Affine almost blowup squares detect h sheaves among fppf sheaves of sets.** An fppf sheaf of
sets whose restriction maps along every affine almost blowup square of the site form a cartesian
square is a sheaf for the h topology.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.isSheaf_of_isFppfSheaf_of_isAffineAlmostBlowUpSheaf`, the
sufficiency direction of Stacks 0EVF for the fppf topology, read on the square-indexed family
`AlgebraicGeometry.AffineAlmostBlowUpSquare`. -/
theorem isAffineAlmostBlowUpDetecting_fppfTopology :
    IsAffineAlmostBlowUpDetecting B S hS (fppfTopology B S hS) := by
  intro G hG
  refine isSheaf_of_isFppfSheaf_of_isAffineAlmostBlowUpSheaf B S hS G.obj G.property ?_
  intro X X' Z E b z p e I haffine hb hZ hpb
  have hfac : p ≫ b = e ≫ z :=
    (BigHOver.toScheme B S hS).map_injective (by
      simp only [Functor.map_comp]
      exact hpb.w.symm)
  exact (hG ⟨Square.mk p e b z hfac, I, haffine, hb, hZ, hpb.flip⟩).flip

end BigHOver

/-! ### Stacks 0EWQ for the fppf topology -/

section

variable (B : BigHSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
  (O : Sheaf (BigHOver.topology B S hS) CommRingCat.{r})
  [HasSheafify (BigHOver.topology B S hS) AddCommGrpCat.{v}]
  [(BigHOver.topology B S hS).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{v}]
  [HasSheafify (BigHOver.fppfTopology B S hS) AddCommGrpCat.{v}]
  [(BigHOver.fppfTopology B S hS).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{v}]
  [UnivLE.{u + 1, v}] [UnivLE.{u, v}] [UnivLE.{r, v}]

/-- **Stacks 0EWQ.** Let `𝒪` be a sheaf of rings for the h topology on the big h category over
`S`, and let `ε : (C_h, 𝒪_h) ⟶ (C_{fppf}, 𝒪_{fppf})` be the comparison of ringed sites given by
the identity functor, the fppf topology on that category being coarser than the h topology.  Then
an object `K` of `D⁺(𝒪_{fppf})` lies in the essential image of the derived direct image `Rε_*` if
and only if the canonical Mayer–Vietoris comparison `c^K_{X,X',Z,E}` of Stacks 0F16 is an
isomorphism for every almost blowup square of the site whose base is affine.

This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.essImageIffAffineAlmostBlowUpBigH_of_isAffineAlmostBlowUpDetecting` at the fppf
topology, where the detection of h sheaves by affine almost blowup squares is
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.isAffineAlmostBlowUpDetecting_fppfTopology`, the sufficiency direction
of Stacks 0EVF. -/
@[stacks 0EWQ]
theorem essImage_iff_forall_isCSquareIso_affineAlmostBlowUp_fppf_bigH :
    EssImageIffAffineAlmostBlowUpBigH.{u, v, r} B S hS O
      (BigHOver.fppfTopology_le_topology B S hS) :=
  essImageIffAffineAlmostBlowUpBigH_of_isAffineAlmostBlowUpDetecting B S hS O
    (BigHOver.fppfTopology_le_topology B S hS)
    (BigHOver.isAffineAlmostBlowUpDetecting_fppfTopology B S hS)

end

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
